  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The most comprehensive open-source library for synthetic tabular data generation — 20+ generative models covering GANs, VAEs, diffusion, and LLM-based methods, with built-in evaluation metrics for privacy, fidelity, and utility. NeurIPS 2023 paper. 664 stars, Apache-2.0, pip-installable. Directly relevant for healthcare teams needing privacy-preserving synthetic EHR data, clinical trial augmentation, or synthetic datasets for model testing. Assess rather than Adopt: pre-1.0 (v0.2.12), no formal clinical validation or regulatory clearance, and does not handle missing data internally (requires separate imputation). Assess for any pipeline requiring synthetic tabular health data — particularly useful where real patient data cannot be shared.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-04",
